            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": {
                "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
                "version": 1,
                "blocks": [
                  {
                    "id": "p23-q21-b-i-answer",
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "fontSize": null,
                    "align": "left",
                    "spaceBefore": 0,
                    "spaceAfter": 2,
                    "lineHeight": 1.4,
                    "indent": 0,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "type": "math",
                        "latex": "g(x)=0.5x",
                        "display": false
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}g(x)&=x-\\frac{50}{100}x\\\\g(x)&=0.5x\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 16
          },
          {
            "id": "p23-q21-b-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "Show that she is incorrect by finding $g(f(x))$.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": {
                "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
                "version": 1,
                "blocks": [
                  {
                    "id": "p23-q21-b-ii-answer",
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "fontSize": null,
                    "align": "left",
                    "spaceBefore": 0,
                    "spaceAfter": 2,
                    "lineHeight": 1.4,
                    "indent": 0,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "type": "math",
                        "latex": "g(f(x))=0.5(1.5x)=0.75x",
                        "display": false
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": ". This does not return the original value, so a 50% decrease does not undo a 50% increase.",
                        "marks": []
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}g(f(x))&=g(1.5x)\\\\g(f(x))&=0.5(1.5x)\\\\g(f(x))&=0.75x\\end{align*}$$\nSince $g(f(x))\\ne x$ in general, $g$ is not the inverse of $f$. A decrease of 50% will not undo an increase of 50%.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 32
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q21-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "What is the inverse function $f^{-1}(x)$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p23-q21-c-answer",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x}{1.5}=\\frac{2x}{3}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=1.5x\\\\x&=1.5y\\\\y&=\\frac{x}{1.5}\\\\y&=\\frac{2x}{3}\\\\f^{-1}(x)&=\\frac{2x}{3}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q21-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Therefore, to undo a 50% increase, what percentage do you need to decrease by?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p23-q21-d-answer",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "33.\\dot{3}\\%",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " decrease: the inverse multiplier is ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\frac{2}{3}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", so decrease by one third.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Since $f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{2}{3}x$, the required decrease is one third of the increased value.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Decrease fraction}&=1-\\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{1}{3}\\\\\\text{Percentage decrease}&=\\frac{1}{3}\\times100\\%=33.\\dot{3}\\%\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      }
    ]
